title: Microsoft Intune: Certificate Connectors
agents: special
catalog: cloud/microsoft
license: GPLv2
distribution: Christopher Pommer
description:
 This check monitors the status of certificate connectors configured in
 Microsoft Intune. Certificate connectors enable Intune to issue certificates
 to managed devices by connecting to on-premises Certificate Authorities (CAs).

 The check processes data collected by the {Microsoft Intune} special agent,
 which queries the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve information about all
 configured certificate connectors in the Intune tenant.

 Certificate connectors must maintain an "active" state to function properly
 and issue certificates to devices. The service monitors connector state:

 {OK}: Connector state is "active"

 {CRIT}: Connector state is any value other than "active"

 The service displays the connector state and version in the summary, with
 detailed information including connector name, unique ID, version, last
 connection time, and current state for administrative reference.

 You must configure the {Microsoft Intune} special agent to collect certificate
 connector data from your Intune tenant.

item:
 The name of the certificate connector as configured in Intune. If multiple
 connectors share the same name, the last 4 characters of the connector ID
 are appended for unique identification (e.g., "Connector1 a1b2").

discovery:
 One service is created automatically for each certificate connector found in
 the Intune tenant. Services are named "Intune connector {connector_name}" where
 {connector_name} is the configured connector name, potentially with ID suffix
 for uniqueness.